span><span>&nbsp;to </span><span style="font-weight:700">Lille</span><span>, </span><span style="font-weight:700">Dino Toppm&ouml;ller</span><span>&nbsp;to </span><span style="font-weight:700">Lens</span><span>, </span><span style="font-weight:700">Will Still</span><span>&nbsp;to </span><span style="font-weight:700">Auxerre</span><span>, </span><span style="font-weight:700">Olivier Pantaloni</span><span>&nbsp;to Nice, </span><span style="font-weight:700">Alexandre Dujeux</span><span>&nbsp;to </span><span style="font-weight:700">Lorient</span><span>. And French football is still absorbing a loss: </span><span style="font-weight:700">&eacute;ric Roy</span><span>, head coach of </span><span style="font-weight:700">Stade Brestois</span><span>, died on 17 June aged 58. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Julien Lachuer</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;has succeeded him. The season&rsquo;s first trophy is on Sunday, when Lens host PSG in the Troph&eacute;e des Champions at Bollaert-Delelis, Lens qualifying as Coupe de France winners.</span></p><h4 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:12pt;padding-bottom:12.8pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#0f2e22;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">United States &middot; Major League Soccer</span></h4><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span>MLS is the only one of the six actually playing, and it has spent the week inside </span><span style="font-weight:700">Leagues Cup</span><span>, which runs from 4 August to a final on 6 September with all thirty-six MLS and Liga MX clubs in two league-wide tables. It has not gone well for the American league. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Vancouver</span><span>&nbsp;and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Minnesota</span><span>&nbsp;are out; </span><span style="font-weight:700">Charlotte</span><span>&nbsp;were eliminated on 11 August by an </span><span style="font-weight:700">Alan Bautista</span><span>&nbsp;goal in the first minute of stoppage time off a miscued </span><span style="font-weight:700">Tim Ream</span><span>&nbsp;pass &mdash; head coach </span><span style="font-weight:700">Dean Smith</span><span>: </span><span style="font-style:italic">&ldquo;a lapse in concentration on the edge of the box cost us everything&rdquo;</span><span>&nbsp;&mdash; and </span><span style="font-weight:700">FC Cincinnati</span><span>&nbsp;effectively bowed out the same night. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Seattle</span><span>, the holders, were beaten 3&ndash;0 at altitude in Toluca on 5 August with </span><span style="font-weight:700">Stefan Frei</span><span>&nbsp;making fourteen saves; </span><span style="font-weight:700">Brian Schmetzer</span><span>&nbsp;was blunt: </span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:italic">&ldquo;Toluca was the better team. The altitude and their intensity hurt us.&rdquo;</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Lionel Messi</span><span>&nbsp;made his first start since the World Cup on 5 August and scored twice in </span><span style="font-weight:700">Inter Miami</span><span>&rsquo;s 4&ndash;2 win over </span><span style="font-weight:700">Atl&eacute;tico de San Luis</span><span>, becoming the competition&rsquo;s all-time leading scorer on fourteen career goals; </span><span style="font-weight:700">Noah Allen</span><span>&nbsp;registered three assists and the match was suspended for around half an hour in the 67th minute for weather. Miami then lost 2&ndash;1 at home to </span><span style="font-weight:700">Monterrey</span><span>&nbsp;on 8 August despite </span><span style="font-weight:700">Rodrigo De Paul</span><span>&rsquo;s goal from a </span><span style="font-weight:700">Casemiro</span><span>&nbsp;assist, both Monterrey scorers being former MLS players, and go into tonight&rsquo;s meeting with </span><span style="font-weight:700">Club Le&oacute;n</span><span>&nbsp;needing to win in regulation to survive. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Luis Su&aacute;rez</span><span>&nbsp;is unavailable, serving a six-game Leagues Cup suspension. Elsewhere </span><span style="font-weight:700">Myrto Uzuni</span><span>&nbsp;scored a first-half hat-trick for </span><span style="font-weight:700">Austin FC</span><span>&nbsp;against </span><span style="font-weight:700">Puebla</span><span>&nbsp;on 9 August, and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Robert Lewandowski</span><span>&nbsp;scored his first goal in the competition for </span><span style="font-weight:700">Chicago</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span>In the league itself &mdash; only one fixture was played in the window, </span><span style="font-weight:700">Houston</span><span>&rsquo;s 2&ndash;0 win at </span><span style="font-weight:700">New England</span><span>&nbsp;on 8 August, their third consecutive clean-sheet victory, and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Jack Harrison</span><span>&rsquo;s Revolution debut. All thirty clubs return on 15&ndash;16 August. Two administrative notes worth filing: </span><span style="font-weight:700">Austin FC</span><span>&nbsp;have promoted </span><span style="font-weight:700">Andy Loughnane</span><span>&nbsp;from club president to chief executive with oversight of both business and soccer, founder </span><span style="font-weight:700">Anthony Precourt</span><span>&nbsp;moving to chairman; and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Mart&iacute; Cifuentes</span><span>&nbsp;has taken over at </span><span style="font-weight:700">Portland</span><span>, bringing assistants </span><span style="font-weight:700">Xavi Calm</span><span>&nbsp;and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Javi Ortiz</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;from Leicester. The wider frame: 2026 is the last full spring&ndash;autumn season, with a one-off fourteen-game &ldquo;Sprint Season&rdquo; from February to May 2027 before the league restarts in July 2027 on a summer&ndash;spring calendar.</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#0f7a4e;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">NUMBERS OF THE WEEK</span></p><h2 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&euro;130m</span></h2><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span>Upper end of the reported base fee for </span><span style="font-weight:700">Yan Diom&aacute;nde</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;&mdash; Real Madrid&rsquo;s biggest signing ever, for a 19-year-old with one top-five-league season behind him.</span></p><h2 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&pound;236m</span></h2><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span>Approximate total raised by </span><span style="font-weight:700">Newcastle</span><span>&nbsp;from selling </span><span style="font-weight:700">Guimar&atilde;es</span><span>, </span><span style="font-weight:700">Tonali</span><span>&nbsp;and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Gordon</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;inside five weeks.</span></p><h2 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">40,000</span></h2><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span>Retro away shirts sold by </span><span style="font-weight:700">Schalke 04</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;in two and a half hours on their return to the Bundesliga.</span></p><h2 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">14</span></h2><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span>Career Leagues Cup goals for </span><span style="font-weight:700">Lionel Messi</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;after his brace on 5 August &mdash; an all-time competition record.</span></p><h2 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&euro;22m</span></h2><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="font-weight:700">Sevilla</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&rsquo;s salary limit &mdash; the lowest in LaLiga, and the reason a European giant is selling to survive.</span></p><h2 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">12 of 20</span></h2><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Premier League clubs starting 2026/27 with a different head coach from the one who ended last season.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#0f7a4e;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">IN BRIEF</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">UEFA changed two rules on 6 August.</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;The yellow-card suspension threshold in all three club competitions rises from three bookings to four &mdash; the rationale being that the expanded league phase guarantees at least eight matches before the knockouts &mdash; and stadium clocks will now count upward through added time rather than freezing at 45:00 and 90:00.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Olympiacos are out of the Champions League.</span><span>&nbsp;</span><span style="font-weight:700">NEC Nijmegen</span><span>&nbsp;beat them 2&ndash;1 after extra time on 11 August to win the tie 2&ndash;1 on aggregate, the biggest scalp of the third qualifying round. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Bod&oslash;/Glimt</span><span>&nbsp;edged </span><span style="font-weight:700">Union Saint-Gilloise</span><span>&nbsp;6&ndash;5 across two legs, and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Lyon</span><span>&nbsp;recovered from a first-leg defeat to beat </span><span style="font-weight:700">Sparta Praha</span><span>&nbsp;4&ndash;2 on aggregate. The play-off round pairs Lyon with </span><span style="font-weight:700">Fenerbah&ccedil;e</span><span>&nbsp;and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Celtic</span><span>&nbsp;with </span><span style="font-weight:700">LASK</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">; the league-phase draw is on 27 August.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Benfica put six past Hearts</span><span>&nbsp;in the Europa League third qualifying round on 6 August, while </span><span style="font-weight:700">Rangers</span><span>&nbsp;lost 2&ndash;1 away to </span><span style="font-weight:700">Jagiellonia Bia&#322;ystok</span><span>&nbsp;and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Maccabi Tel-Aviv</span><span>&nbsp;were beaten 3&ndash;0 at home by </span><span style="font-weight:700">CSKA Sofia</span><span>. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Ajax</span><span>, meanwhile, are in Conference League qualifying, where they beat </span><span style="font-weight:700">Shelbourne</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;3&ndash;1.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">The Saudi Pro League season starts on Thursday.</span><span>&nbsp;</span><span style="font-weight:700">Cristiano Ronaldo</span><span>, now 41, begins it on 976 career goals &mdash; twenty-four short of a thousand &mdash; having scored 28 as </span><span style="font-weight:700">Al Nassr</span><span>&nbsp;won the title. Nine SPL clubs changed manager over the summer; </span><span style="font-weight:700">Ange Postecoglou</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;is now in charge at Al Nassr.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Paul Pogba is a free agent.</span><span>&nbsp;</span><span style="font-weight:700">Monaco</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;v